\pard\intbl Rab\cell ...... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell So auld King Gustaf's no more... Ach, it's a real shame. He was a wise, unflappable ruler who loved his people well, and was well-loved in turn.\par
\par
And now a wicked witch has brought his kingdom to its knees... We have to give her what for and save this place\f1\emdash\f0 for Gus's sake. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell If we don't save Sniflheim, Queen Frysabel will be left all on her lonesome, the poor wee thing.\par
\par
We've got to get rid of that rotten witch as quick as we can, and put this kingdom back on its feet. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Och, it's a wee bit chillier round here now than it was before. I'll warrant it's got something to do with that witch getting her powers back.\par
\par
Aye, we made a bit of a blunder beating up that magical beast, didn't we? What was Queen Frysabel thinking, telling us it was in league with the witch? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Whoever would have thought that Queen Frysabel was Krystalinda all along...? That wicked witch certainly gave us the runaround, and no mistake.\par
\par
Still, we managed to see through her little disguise eventually, and bunged her back in the book for good measure. All's well that ends well, as they say. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Krystalinda's tale about the young man freeing her from the book doesnae bode well, but at least we got our hands on the Blue Orb.\par
\par
Now, it's high time we were moving on. Lead the way, laddie! \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Listen, laddie\f1\emdash\f0 ye've got this whole mucky magazine business the wrong way round. Those things go for silly money! I wasnae going to read it\f1\emdash\f0 I was going to sell it and help fund the restoration of Dundrasil!\par
\par
Imagine that, eh? Risking personal humiliation, and all to help rebuild the kingdom we love! If ye ask me, you lot owe me an apology! \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell It's been a fair wee while since last I set foot in this castle. Aye, I reckon it was back when me and auld King Gustaf still had full heads of hair! Happy days... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell First we find out that Her Majesty was the wicked witch in disguise yet again, and now it looks like the real queen's in cahoots with her!\par
\par
Can somebody please explain to me what in blue blazes is going on around here!? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell It's a ruler's duty to stand in the vanguard and lead from the front. I've been there myself, so I know what I'm saying when I tell ye that the burden resting on Queen Frysabel's shoulders is a weighty one indeed.\par
\par
I reckon the lassie can handle it, though\f1\emdash\f0 after all, she's her father's daughter. She's as wise and as prudent as auld King Gustaf, and his father before him.\par
\par
No, there's no need to worry about this place going down the nick again. With Queen Frysabel in charge, Sniflheim's sure to go from strength to strength! \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell The Blue Orb's one of the Sniflheimian royal family's most precious treasures. It's locked up tight in the castle vaults.\par
\par
We've no chance of getting our mitts on it till the ice around the castle is gone. What do ye say we go and have a word with that witch? See if we can't...persuade her to dispel her magic? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell I've heard Snorri's name before, ye know. Aye, he's quite the celebrity among Sniflheimian scholars.\par
\par
If he can find what he's looking for in the Royal Library, we might just be able to figure a way to save this kingdom. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell If what that book Snorri found in the library said is true, then we've been looking at this whole situation topsy-turvy.\par
\par
I'm still not entirely sure what's going on around here, but if anyone can tell us, it's the Queen. What do ye say we go back to Sniflheim and have a heart-to-heart with the wee lassie? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell The Blue Orb's one of the Sniflheimian royal family's most precious treasures. It's locked up tight in the castle vaults.\par
\par
Queen Frysabel said she'd let us have it as a reward for saving Sniflheim. Let's head on over to the castle before she changes her mind, shall we? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Sniflheim should be safe in Queen Frysabel's hands. Aye, the lassie's got a wise head on those young shoulders.\par
\par
