\par
Well laddie, it's time to take on the Wheel of Harma. No one's managed it since Erdwin himself, so it's going to be a stiff challenge. I know we can do it, though\f1\emdash\f0 let's show Grand Master Pang what we've got!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell Ah, it's good to be back in Angri-La. This is where Erdwin once took on the supreme challenge of the Wheel of Harma, ye know.\par
\par
Now, there's a training area called the Field of Discipline on the other side of the High Hall. Ye'll usually find folk honing their minds and bodies in there.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell I was just a wee bairn when I first came to Angri-La, so this is a real trip down memory lane for me.\par
\par
...Oh, hang on a sec! I just remembered something! There's this funny-looking tree near the entrance to the village...\par
\par
Now I come to think of it, it looks a wee bit like the sacred seedlings in the Watchers' temple.\par
\par
I reckon it'd be worth our while taking a look at it, laddie. Ye never know...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10340 
\pard\intbl Rab\cell The peak of Mount Pang Lai is a very spiritual place. It's said to be close to the void, the borderland that separates the worlds of the living and the dead.\par
\par
